65:Static Friction and Kinetic Friction Physics Problems With Free Body Diagrams,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RIBeeW1DSZg,"Explains static and kinetic friction, their dependence on applied force and normal force, and how to use free-body diagrams and Newton’s laws to calculate acceleration."
67:Calculating Contact Forces Between Two Blocks Using Free Body Diagrams,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Iin29KFE4So,Uses free-body diagrams and Newton’s third law to calculate contact forces between two blocks with and without kinetic friction.
68:Tension Force Physics Problems,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=F5oqJ5t-pa4,"Works through tension problems involving a descending object and two-rope or two-cable systems at different angles using Newton’s laws, weight, and free-body diagrams."
72:Introduction to Inclined Planes,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ufgY237M5KQ,"Covers inclined-plane equations and free-body diagrams for normal force, gravity parallel to the incline, kinetic friction, net force, and acceleration."
75:The Pulley - Simple Machines,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GAegAHnfkMs,Introduces the pulley as a simple machine that provides mechanical advantage through tension in a rope.
76:Pulley Physics Problem - Finding Acceleration and Tension Force,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N6IhkTjWrd4,"Works through pulley systems with two masses, calculating acceleration, rope tension, effects of kinetic friction, direction of motion, and cases with hanging masses or inclined planes."
77:"Static & Kinetic Friction, Tension, Normal Force, Inclined Plane & Pulley System Problems - Physics",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pL2YfC-22Uc,"Covers static and kinetic friction, tension, normal force, inclined-plane forces, and pulley systems."
82:Tetherball Physics Problem - Calculate Tension Force,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G0RikmNonoU,"Works through a tetherball free-body diagram, relating the horizontal tension component to centripetal force and the vertical component to the ball's weight."
86:Banked turn Physics Problems,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FWXT-IzgbP0,"Works through frictionless banked-turn free-body diagrams and derives relationships among vehicle speed, banking angle, and the minimum and maximum speeds that prevent sliding."
135:"Torque, Basic Introduction, Lever Arm, Moment of Force, Simple Machines & Mechanical Advantage",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jg4e8W44_E4,"Introduces torque, lever arms, rotational sign conventions, and the mechanical advantage of simple machines such as seesaws and shovels."
137:"Inertia - Basic Introduction, Torque, Angular Acceleration, Newton's Second Law, Rotational Motion",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ic_wFYu8xVs,"Introduces translational and rotational inertia, relates force and torque laws, and explains how mass distribution determines the moments of inertia of hoops, disks, and point masses."
139:Rotational Dynamics - Basic Introduction,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dbvr-L5rxdg,"Introduces rotational dynamics through hanging masses and rotating pulleys, including Atwood machines and inclined planes with kinetic friction."
140:Rotational Kinetic Energy and Moment of Inertia Examples & Physics Problems,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=REIP2mf6sIQ,Uses energy conservation and rotational dynamics to calculate speeds for rolling objects on inclines and falling blocks attached to rotating pulleys.
145:Angular Momentum Physics Practice Problems,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QghXDDJtJeQ,"Works through angular-momentum problems involving a disk, a rotating rod, torque, angular speed, work, and a child jumping onto a merry-go-round."
147:"Torque, Moment of Inertia, Rotational Kinetic Energy, Pulley, Incline, Angular Acceleration, Physics",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SPSvosj6Snc,"Reviews angular displacement, velocity and acceleration, torque, moment of inertia, rotational kinetic energy, and the parallel-axis theorem through pulley, incline, and friction problems."
170:"Archimedes Principle, Buoyant Force, Basic Introduction - Buoyancy & Density - Fluid Statics",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Qgl_l0H7Qgc,"Introduces Archimedes' principle, derives the buoyant-force formula, and uses free-body diagrams to calculate tension on a submerged block."
174:How To Calculate The Fractional Volume Submerged & The Density of an Object In Two Fluids,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sMkHKMsBEl8,Uses Archimedes' principle and free-body diagrams to calculate the submerged fraction and density of an object floating between oil and water.
177:"Continuity Equation, Volume Flow Rate & Mass Flow Rate Physics Problems",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DxX6XLEdcAw,"Introduces the continuity equation and solves for fluid velocity, mass flow rate, and volume flow rate when a pipe's cross-sectional area changes."
204:"Thermal Stress and Strain - Basic Introduction - Compressive & Tensile Forces, Elastic Modulus",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FwOsoeOvZzo,"Explains thermal stress and strain under temperature changes, including compressive and tensile forces and calculations involving Young's modulus, cross-sectional area, linear expansion, and temperature change."
255:"Electric Flux, Gauss's Law & Electric Fields, Through a Cube, Sphere, & Disk, Physics Problems",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q1eor6oIuUo,"Explains electric flux and Gauss's law, calculates flux through disks, squares, spheres, and cubes, and distinguishes inward from outward flux and the relevant angle conventions."
277:"Resistivity and Resistance Formula, Conductivity, Temperature Coefficient, Physics Problems",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PIJTu8z0-_U,"Explains resistivity, resistance, and conductivity in conductors and semiconductors, including their dependence on material, temperature, wire length, and cross-sectional area and their use in temperature measurement."
282:Potential Difference Between Two Points In an Electric Field - Current Density & Resistivity,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vcbkvYDP5a8,"Calculates potential difference between points on a conductor using electric field, resistivity, current density, cross-sectional area, and distance."
304:Electron Flow In Capacitors During Charging & Discharging - Physics,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iQZknlJjaj4,"Explains electron flow during capacitor charging and discharging, including why electrons move between plates through the circuit rather than across an intact dielectric."
317:"Magnetic Field of a Moving Charge, Proton, Right Hand Rule - Physics & Electromagnetism",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CXChim2gOzs,Calculates the magnetic field produced by a moving charge and determines its direction using the right-hand rule and the cross product of velocity and position vectors.
322:"Lenz's Law, Right Hand Rule, Induced Current, Electromagnetic Induction - Physics",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HhFZfWLl-P0,Explains Lenz's law and uses it with the right-hand rule to determine the direction of induced current.
333:RL Circuits - Inductors & Resistors,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RR0sQeDAxgk,"Covers RL circuits, including instantaneous and maximum current, time constants, voltages across the resistor and inductor, energy-consumption rates, and induced EMF from changing current."

